{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // Mirrors apps/api exactly, and has to: this package imports that app's
    // source directly (the prompt and the schema the gate measures), so a
    // different module resolution here would typecheck a different program
    // from the one that ships.
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler",
    "noEmit": true,
    // ⚠ Needed since the coding gate (6 Sep 2026), and not decoration: the
    // coding ladder's chart service reaches `clients-team-settings`' public
    // seam, whose barrel carries Nest controllers. `tsx` transforms through
    // esbuild, which reads THIS file, and without the flag the whole run dies
    // with "Parameter decorators only work when experimental decorators are
    // enabled" pointing at a controller no eval calls. `apps/api` has it on;
    // this line is the mirror the comment above already promises.
    "experimentalDecorators": true,
    "emitDecoratorMetadata": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  // ⚠ **The WHOLE of `apps/api/src`, and it is `tsx` that requires it rather
  // than `tsc`.** esbuild applies a tsconfig's options only to files that
  // tsconfig actually MATCHES, so a transitively-imported file outside this
  // list is transformed with no options at all — which is how the coding gate
  // first died on "Parameter decorators only work when experimental decorators
  // are enabled", pointing at a Nest controller no eval calls. The coding
  // ladder's chart service reaches `clients-team-settings`' public seam, that
  // barrel reaches `notifications`', and that one exports a controller.
  //
  // Listing the tree is the honest fix: this package really does execute that
  // code, and a narrower list would only mean the compiler checks less of what
  // the runner runs.
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "../apps/api/src/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", ".turbo"]
}
